  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A coil is placed in magnetic field such that plane of coil is perpendicular to the direction of magnetic field. The magnetic flux through a coil can be changed:</p><p>A. By changing the magnitude of the magnetic field within the coil.</p><p>B. By changing the area of coil within the magnetic field.</p><p>C. By changing the angle between the direction of magnetic field and the plane of the coil.</p><p>D. By reversing the magnetic field direction abruptly without changing its magnitude.</p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "I7LVq",
      "text": "A and B only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6rPhw",
      "text": "A, B and C only",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tQ3Y1",
      "text": "A, B and D only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "siQpo",
      "text": "A and C only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Magnetic flux through a coil is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>.</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math>, where,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>is&nbsp;magnetic field, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;area of coil and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;the angle between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.</p><p>Thus, from above expression, we can say that magnetic flux can&nbsp;be changed by changing magnetic field, area of coil, change the angle between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, correct&nbsp;options are A, B and C.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
